Give the fork its own Tauri identifier so it coexists with stock Handy on the
REAL session D-Bus bus. With the shared "com.pais.handy" identity the patched
instance had to hide inside dbus-run-session to dodge tauri-plugin-single-instance
— which also hid its tray icon (StatusNotifierItem never reached KDE's watcher)
and swallowed its notifications, making the app look like it never launched.
A distinct identifier gives it its own single-instance D-Bus name AND its own
data dir (com.pais.handy.patched), so the launcher needs no private bus and no
XDG_DATA_HOME override. Applies on top of patches 01-03.

--- a/src-tauri/tauri.conf.json
+++ b/src-tauri/tauri.conf.json
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
   "$schema": "https://schema.tauri.app/config/2",
   "productName": "Handy",
   "version": "0.8.3",
-  "identifier": "com.pais.handy",
+  "identifier": "com.pais.handy.patched",
   "build": {
     "beforeDevCommand": "bun run dev",
     "devUrl": "http://localhost:1420",
